summary:
  The order's deadline applies to an alarm's standing order too, so a
  wake-up whose station was down overnight ends in silence.

history:
  Issue #13, read against the code a third time on 2026-09-21. The knock
  budget is counted on QML timers, and those stand still while the machine
  sleeps: a station that goes quiet at eleven with the lid closed a minute
  later still has knocks left at eight the next morning, and the network
  coming back replays it — nine hours late, under the release whose notes
  said nothing could put it back on. The relay road can leave the order
  standing with no ladder at all. Both arrive through _replayOrder, which now
  asks the wall clock before it plays.

target:
  package/contents/ui/RetryLogic.js

find:
  function orderExpired(sinceMs, nowMs, exempt, cap) {
      if (exempt === true) return false;

replace:
  function orderExpired(sinceMs, nowMs, exempt, cap) {
      if (exempt === 1) return false;

expect:
  Killed by tst_retrylogic::test_an_alarm_never_expires_and_neither_does_keep_trying_forever.
  Line-neutral.
